mixin () {
  // Static, source-derived documentation of the public backend API.
  // No state is read; the Markdown literal is returned directly.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# AdixLoop Backend API\n\nAdixLoop is a short-form vertical video (Reels) social app. This canister stores\nuser profiles, reels, comments, likes, follows, an activity inbox, a wallet with\ntransactions, and per-user drafts. It also exposes its persisted collections to\nthe Caffeine Data Intelligence agent through the OQL `schema()` / `execute()`\nquery endpoints.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- The app's frontend authenticates with Internet Identity and pins an\n  Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n  `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already\n  holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app\n  principal against that origin (for example\n  `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the\n  user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Most read endpoints are public queries and work for anonymous callers.\n- Endpoints marked **caller-scoped** below read or write the caller's own data.\n  They key on the caller principal directly and do not require prior\n  registration. The backend does not itself reject anonymous callers on these\n  endpoints; the app's frontend gates them behind Internet Identity sign-in, so\n  an anonymous caller would operate on the anonymous principal's own (empty)\n  data.\n- The authorization mixin adds role management. `_initialize_access_control()`\n  registers the caller: the first non-anonymous caller to invoke it becomes\n  `#admin`, every later caller becomes `#user`. `getCallerUserRole()` returns\n  `#guest` for an anonymous caller and traps with `User is not registered` for a\n  signed-in principal that never registered. `assignCallerUserRole(user, role)`\n  is admin-only and traps with `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles`\n  otherwise. `isCallerAdmin()` reports whether the caller is an admin.\n- A caller can be signed in yet unregistered: registration happens only when a\n  principal calls `_initialize_access_control()` (the app's frontend does this\n  during sign-in). A principal that never signed in through this app's frontend\n  is unregistered even if it belongs to the app's owner, and a principal derived\n  against a different derivation origin is a different principal than the one\n  the frontend registered.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `Timestamp` is `Int`, nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`).\n- `UserId` is a `Principal`. `ReelId`, `CommentId`, `TransactionId`, and\n  `DraftId` are `Nat`.\n- `Audience` is `{ #everyone; #followers }`.\n- `TransactionKind` is `{ #reelBonus; #referralBonus; #withdrawal }`.\n- `TransactionStatus` is `{ #pending; #completed; #failed }`.\n- `ActivityKind` is `{ #like; #comment; #follow; #mention }`.\n- Optional fields (`?Text`, `?Nat`) are Candid `opt`; absent values are `null`.\n- Monetary amounts (`balance`, `amount`, `reelEarnings`, `referralEarnings`) are\n  `Nat` in the app's internal unit; no currency conversion is performed.\n- Mutations return a variant result: `{ #ok : T }` on success or\n  `{ #err : E }` with a typed error. Errors are never returned as `Text`.\n\n## Profiles\n\n- `createProfile(username, displayName, bio, avatarUrl)` — **caller-scoped**.\n  Creates the caller's profile. Usernames are trimmed and lowercased, must be\n  3–30 characters of `a-z`, `A-Z`, `0-9`, `_`, or `.`, and must be unique.\n  Errors: `#usernameTaken`, `#invalidUsername`. A caller may create only one\n  profile; a second call returns `#usernameTaken`.\n- `getProfile(user)` — public. Returns `?UserProfile` or `null`.\n- `getProfileByUsername(username)` — public. Case-insensitive lookup.\n- `updateProfile(update)` — **caller-scoped**. `update` is\n  `{ displayName : ?Text; username : ?Text; bio : ?Text; avatarUrl : ?Text }`;\n  `null` fields are left unchanged. Errors: `#notFound`, `#invalidUsername`,\n  `#usernameTaken`.\n- `getUserSummary(user)` — public. Returns `?UserSummary` with follower and\n  following counts and whether the caller follows `user`.\n\n## Reels\n\n- `createReel(input)` — **caller-scoped**. `input` is\n  `{ mediaUrl; thumbnailUrl : ?Text; caption; hashtags : [Text];\n  soundLabel : ?Text; location : ?Text; audience; allowComments; allowDuet }`.\n  Returns `{ #ok : Reel }` or `{ #err : ReelError }`. Hashtags and the sound\n  label are indexed for search.\n- `getReel(id)` — public. Returns `?ReelView` with like/comment counts.\n- `listReelsByUser(user)` — public. Newest first.\n- `listForYouFeed()` — public. All reels, newest first.\n- `listFollowingFeed()` — **caller-scoped**. Reels from accounts the caller\n  follows, newest first.\n\n## Likes and comments\n\n- `toggleReelLike(reelId)` — **caller-scoped**. Toggles the caller's like and\n  returns `{ #ok : Bool }` where `true` means now liked. Errors: `#notFound`.\n  Liking another user's reel records an inbox activity for that user.\n- `getReelLikeState(reelId)` — public. Returns `{ likeCount; isLiked }`.\n- `toggleCommentLike(commentId)` — **caller-scoped**. Toggles the caller's comment\n  like. Errors: `#notFound`.\n- `addComment(reelId, text)` — **caller-scoped**. Returns\n  `{ #ok : CommentView }` or `{ #err : SocialError }`. Errors: `#notFound`\n  (reel missing) and `#notAuthorized` (comments disabled on the reel).\n  Commenting on another user's reel records an inbox activity.\n- `listComments(reelId)` — public. Oldest first.\n\n## Follows\n\n- `follow(user)` — **caller-scoped**. Errors: `#cannotFollowSelf`. Records an inbox\n  activity for `user`.\n- `unfollow(user)` — **caller-scoped**. Errors: `#cannotFollowSelf`.\n- `getFollowState(user)` — public. Returns\n  `{ followerCount; followingCount; isFollowing }`.\n- `listFollowers(user)` — public. Returns `[Principal]`.\n- `listFollowing(user)` — public. Returns `[Principal]`.\n\n## Search\n\n- `search(filter, term)` — public. `filter` is\n  `{ #all; #users; #reels; #sounds; #hashtags }`. Matching is case-insensitive\n  substring matching over usernames/display names, reel captions/hashtags/sound\n  labels, and the sound and hashtag indexes. Returns\n  `{ users : [UserId]; reels : [ReelId]; sounds : [SoundResult];\n  hashtags : [HashtagResult] }`.\n- `trendingHashtags(limit)` — public. Hashtags ordered by reel count, capped at\n  `limit`.\n- `reelsByHashtag(tag)` — public. Case-insensitive; returns `[ReelId]`.\n- `reelsBySound(soundLabel)` — public. Case-insensitive; returns `[ReelId]`.\n\n## Inbox\n\n- `listActivity(kind)` — **caller-scoped**. Returns the caller's activity, newest\n  first. `kind` is `?ActivityKind`; `null` returns every kind.\n\n## Wallet\n\n- `getWallet()` — **caller-scoped**. Returns the caller's `Wallet`\n  (`balance`, `reelEarnings`, `referralEarnings`, `referralCode`). A wallet is\n  created lazily on first read.\n- `listTransactions()` — **caller-scoped**. Newest first.\n- `requestWithdrawal(request)` — **caller-scoped**. `request` is\n  `{ upiId : Text; amount : Nat }`. Errors: `#invalidAmount` (zero),\n  `#invalidUpiId` (empty or missing `@`), `#insufficientBalance`. On success the\n  amount is deducted immediately and a `#withdrawal` transaction with status\n  `#pending` is recorded. Withdrawals are recorded only; no real payout is\n  performed.\n\n## Drafts\n\n- `saveDraft(draftId, input)` — **caller-scoped**. `draftId` is `?Nat`: `null`\n  creates a new draft, a value updates an existing one. Errors: `#notFound`,\n  `#notAuthorized` (not the owner). Returns `{ #ok : Draft }`.\n- `listDrafts()` — **caller-scoped**. The caller's drafts, most recently updated\n  first.\n- `deleteDraft(draftId)` — **caller-scoped**. Errors: `#notFound`, `#notAuthorized`.\n\n## OQL data access\n\n- `schema()` — returns a JSON schema document of the queryable entities the\n  caller may read.\n- `execute(qJson)` — runs a JSON query and returns typed rows. Authorization is\n  per entity: `user`, `reel`, `comment`, `reelLike`, `commentLike`, and `follow`\n  are world-readable; `activity`, `transaction`, and `draft` are scoped to the\n  caller's own rows (controllers read all). Anonymous callers are denied scoped\n  entities.\n\n## Lifecycle, polling, and retry safety\n\n- All reads are `query` calls and are safe to poll; they never mutate state.\n- `createReel`, `addComment`, `follow`, `toggleReelLike`, `toggleCommentLike`,\n  `requestWithdrawal`, `saveDraft`, and `deleteDraft` are update calls.\n- `toggleReelLike` and `toggleCommentLike` are **not idempotent**: each call\n  flips the current state, so a retried call reverses the first. Read the\n  current like state (`getReelLikeState` for reels) before retrying.\n- `follow` and `unfollow` are idempotent (adding/removing a set membership).\n- `createProfile` is not idempotent: a retry after success returns\n  `#usernameTaken`.\n- `createReel`, `addComment`, and `saveDraft` with `draftId = null` append a new\n  record on every call; a retry creates a duplicate. Pass the returned id back\n  to `saveDraft` to update instead.\n- `requestWithdrawal` deducts the balance on success; a retry after a successful\n  call will deduct again if the balance still covers it. Confirm via\n  `listTransactions()` before retrying.\n- `deleteDraft` is idempotent in effect but a retry after success returns\n  `#notFound`.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Errors are typed variants, never `Text`; branch on the variant tag.\n- `getCallerUserRole()` traps for a signed-in but unregistered principal.\n- `assignCallerUserRole` traps for non-admins.\n- `addComment` returns `#notAuthorized` when the reel has comments disabled.\n- `requestWithdrawal` validates the UPI id only syntactically (non-empty and\n  containing `@`); no real payment is made.\n- `getWallet()` creates a wallet as a side effect of a `query` call; because\n  query state changes are discarded, the wallet is recreated on the next read.\n- Timestamps are nanoseconds; divide by 1_000_000 for milliseconds.\n";
  };
};
